course: dictionary
lesson: 13613
title: Working independently
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Independently is an adverb, so it tells you how someone does something. It means on your own, without help from others. «Mia can tie her shoes independently now.» Mia does not need anyone to help her, so she ties them by herself.
explain: The word has a useful pattern. Depend means need or rely on something. Independent means not needing or relying on something, so independently means in that free way. «Work independently» is a phrase you will hear at school. It means do the task yourself, without copying.
explain: The same word appears in science and maths too. «Two scientists independently discovered the same thing» means each of them found it alone, not by copying the other. In probability, «independent events do not affect each other»: a coin landing heads does not change what a dice shows next.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If "on your own" fits in place of "independently" and the sentence still makes sense, you have it right.
fact: Independently means on your own, without help.
fact: «Work independently» means do the task yourself, without copying.
fact: Independently of something means not connected to it and not affected by it.
fact: In maths, «independent events» are events that do not affect each other.
fact: Independent can also describe a country that rules itself, not ruled by another country.
exercise: «Mia can tie her shoes independently now.» What does independently mean? | Very quickly and neatly | Sadly, after a long day | Tightly, with a bow | *On her own, without help
exercise: Ben's teacher says, «Work independently.» What should Ben do? | *Do the task himself, without copying | Ask his friend to do it for him | Wait until the bell rings | Read a book about birds
exercise: Which meaning is closest to independently? | Happily, with a big smile | Loudly, in a crowd | Last of all, after everyone else | *Separately, not affected by something else
test: «The two scientists independently discovered the same thing.» What does this mean? | *Each found it alone, without copying the other | They found it together, sharing every idea | They never found it at all | They found it by accident in the park
test: In maths, what does «independent events» mean? | Events that last a very long time | *Events that do not affect each other | Events that always happen at the same time | Events that happen only once
exam: Which word means "on your own, without help from others"? | Together | *Independently | Carelessly | Dependently
